{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 13, :comments ["<b>And you, speak to the children of Israel.</b> 'And you' — even though I have charged you to command them concerning the work of the Mishkan, let it not be light in your eyes to push aside the Sabbath on account of that work." "<b>However, My Sabbaths you shall keep.</b> Even though you will be hard-pressed and zealous in the zeal of the work, let the Sabbath not be set aside because of it — every אַכִין וְרַקִּין is diminished, i.e., to set aside the Sabbath from the work of the Mishkan." "<b>For it is a sign between Me and you.</b> It is a great sign between us, that I chose you in causing you to inherit My day of rest for rest." "<b>to know.</b> The nations through it <b>that I am YHWH who sanctifies you.</b>"], :book :exodus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {1 "אַכִין וְרַקִּין is a talmudic idiom meaning 'even things joined (אתחקן/אתעקר)'; here: every form of work that is joined and uprooted is diminished before Shabbat."}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T08:56:00.698058836Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}